views.sample_query:
SELECT days_out, target_fill, median_share
FROM mart.segment_curves
WHERE segment = 'local / flu season / one-day' AND days_out IN (180, 90, 30, 0);

SELECT strategy, SUM(outreach_units) AS units
FROM mart.outreach_plan
GROUP BY strategy;

docs.text:
Benchmarks from completed sessions - target fill rate (60th percentile, never decreasing), median share of final appointments, volatility and cancellation survival. Grain: one row per segment and days_out. Columns: segment: demand segment; days_out: days to session; target_fill: target fill rate at this days_out; median_fill: median historical fill rate; median_share: median share of final appointments already booked; share_std: standard deviation of share of final (volatility); survival: median net / gross ratio; n_sessions: number of past sessions supporting the benchmark. SELECT days_out, target_fill, median_share
FROM mart.segment_curves
WHERE segment = 'local / flu season / one-day' AND days_out IN (180, 90, 30, 0);

Extra appointments that must come from outreach campaigns, allocated over the remaining window by strategy (baseline or milestones). Only sessions that pass the eligibility rules get a plan. Grain: one row per eligible session, strategy and days_out. Columns: session_id: session identifier; strategy: baseline or milestones; days_out: days to session; outreach_units: extra appointments planned for this days_out. SELECT strategy, SUM(outreach_units) AS units
FROM mart.outreach_plan
GROUP BY strategy;
